 "calculus-differential-equations": "differential equation|An equation involving a function and its derivatives.|y′ = 3y;general solution|A family of solutions with an arbitrary constant.|y = Ce^(3x);particular solution|The solution that meets an initial condition.|y = 2e^(3x) with y(0) = 2;initial condition|A known value of the solution at a point.|y(0) = 5;slope field|Short segments showing y′ at many points.|A picture of a differential equation;Euler's method|Approximating a solution with tangent-line steps.|yₙ₊₁ = yₙ + h·f(xₙ, yₙ);separation of variables|Moving all y terms to one side and x terms to the other.|(1/y) dy = k dx;exponential growth model|y′ = ky has solutions y = Ce^(kt).|Population growth;Newton's Law of Cooling|T′ = -k(T - Tₐ).|Coffee cooling to room temperature;exponential decay model|dy/dt = ky with k < 0: the amount shrinks by a constant percent.|Radioactive decay;logistic growth|Growth that slows as the quantity approaches a carrying capacity.|dP/dt = kP(1 - P/L);equilibrium solution|A constant solution where the derivative is zero.|y = 0 for dy/dx = 2y",
